  "scope": "v313 adds a stable refinery-nearest-miner selection button, shared count/cohort logic, and exact new button subtree projection. Existing gameplay commands and economic rules remain unchanged. v312 suppresses repeated Escape keydown in the existing global repeat guard only; first Escape, other keys, native focused controls and gameplay rules remain unchanged. No new DOM projection. v311 adds low-contrast ground remnants only for depleted ore. Positive ore commands and all world rules remain unchanged; explicit ground-paint expected-side compatibility preserves prior assertions. No new DOM projection. v310 adds five building identification thumbnails at common scale, with decorative markup and read-only existing-toggle sync. Existing vehicle gallery and battlefield draw functions unchanged. Exact buildingReferenceGallery subtree is the sole new DOM projection. v309 adds a static five-vehicle recognition gallery to the existing folded reference. Exact captured original/preview SVG art, scoped CSS and read-only mode synchronization; exact uniquely attached vehicleReferenceGallery subtree is the sole new DOM projection; all old text and gameplay retained. Strict inverse preserves v308 and earlier history. v308 distinguishes no living factory from unfinished factory and paused construction in new-purchase refusal feedback; guard predicates and queue/economy unchanged. Exact v307 inverse and historical files retained. v307 changes only insufficient-funds purchase receipt plus version. Exact buy predicates, queue, cash and input rules retained; strict v306 inverse preserves all history. v306 adds read-only inline construction-card reasons. Exact disabled predicate, prices and time retained. Strict v305 inverse and frozen verification retained. v305 preserves only a valid unreleased same-battle enabled Space-key token for all-factories selection during repeats; other token cancellation, Escape and visibility semantics stay unchanged. Strict v304 inverse and frozen verification are retained. v304 adds only F/I/M to the existing repeated-key suppression list and display version. Current suites execute the actual v313 source; exact reviewed inverse preserves all v303 and older identity checks. Original suites retain their assertions and no new DOM projection is added. v303 changes only sub-1000 ore map labels to upward-rounded integers and display version. Expected-side historical layout replay uses independently specified new strings and measurement metrics, preserving all layout/clamp/fallback logic; candidate paint streams are untouched. v302 changes only ore decorative block count to 1/4/8 at 1500/4500 thresholds and display version. Exact ore-tail projection validates unchanged base, retained sequence, styles, labels and all other commands; no new DOM exclusion. v301 adds four canonical preview-building team cues and exact in-preview explanatory text; default-off branch and world logic unchanged. Current paint expectations project only strictly validated exact marker groups and preserve all other paints/path/method/world behavior; no new DOM exclusion. v300 adds only the default-closed read-only beginnerSurvivalGuide subtree plus version, with exact whole JS/CSS equality to v299. New root-only inherited projection preserves all existing controls and fields. v299 clarifies global repeat-mode scope using exact template additions and two receipt strings; scheduling and shared thresholds unchanged. v298 adds only exact hold guidance template text and attributes; inline gameplay script stays byte-identical to v297. New projections normalize only exact known added attributes and two hint roots, with independent retained-field boundary controls. v297 clamps only negative shared health-bar y to zero; existing nonnegative positions and gameplay unchanged. Natural pointer-command tanks prove partial 3.8-to-4-pixel visibility; fully hidden thresholds are synthetic. v296 moves shared factory/construction rails fully within unchanged clipping rectangles; only four y offsets and version change. New current renderer comparisons normalize exact expected historical rail offsets, with focused full-intersection/state coverage and semantic mutants. v295 extends the default-off preview to buildings; three authoritative source edits and version-only bump, no gameplay change, no new DOM projection exclusions. v294 adds a default-off session-only vehicle-art preview and per-call lazy ore-label box reuse. Legacy drawUnit stays exact, experimental cached/fallback full-frame paint and default baseline parity are separate from performance claims. A single displayPreview subtree is additionally projected with retained-field boundary tests. v293 adds only one quick-mission preset and tactical brief; exact new button/brief subtree exclusions and exact seven-item text normalization are boundary-tested. v292 ignores repeated group digit keys while preserving first keys and visible clicks; its inherited group-protection test changes only the repeat-save expectation and adds a fresh-key assertion. Frozen v291 files and exact restoration retained. Persistent receipt adds existing allocation-failure counts only; exact v290 restoration and frozen v290 verification preserved. Intentional empty-group protection and live-only saved membership, with frozen v289 files and exact v289 restoration. Current-source VM behavior/markup and source checks are counted separately from exact restored-v272 identities. Two named inherited DOM comparators use hash-locked temporary adapters that omit only coordinateCommandPanel, selectionRemovePanel, postSelectionPanel and coordinateConstructionPanel subtrees plus marked detached OPTION nodes; v281 additionally excludes only patrolActionHint and patrol text/title/aria-describedby, all separately tested; v282 additionally excludes only globalRepeatScopeHint and repeatProduction aria-label/title/aria-describedby, also separately tested; v283 additionally excludes only the new selectAllFactories button subtree, with direct removal and retained-control boundary checks. v284 changes only equal-value order-display string writes; v285 adds a per-updateOrders lazy shared waiting-reason supplier. v286 suppresses equal-value writes for the existing selection-filter button text/title strings. v287 suppresses equal-value writes for the existing battle-report cells, ten action labels and unit/build card titles. v288 reuses one local completed-building list within each power call. v284-v288 add no DOM exclusions. v289 additionally excludes only openingPractice and descendants, with exact prior-projection reversal, physical removal equivalence and retained-field boundaries; a separate opening-practice suite directly covers its content and behavior. All projections rebuild indexes. All 25 programs execute against this actual v313 source; packaged old tests and VM remain byte-identical. Fifteen old source gates intentionally reject v313; only the frozen case name, failure shape and error first line are allowed. No browser or save/load/import/export execution.",
